-- title:
--   Original BVA96 exact compensated marked-jump plus ruin-contact cash error has explicit nonnegative integrable canonical spatial witness and pathwise budget
-- statement:
--   For the genuine original bounded-variation infinite-activity spectrally negative Levy process and the actual admissible dividend strategy, with the source exact prescribed uniform-grid cash and full-horizon survivor terminal F, row-specific spatially masked negative-jump count-minus-compensator noise N, and genuine clipped open-interval Stieltjes ruin-contact cash, define the canonical signed spatial remainder ErrSpatial=F-(w(x)+N)-Contact. Prove its positive part is integrable at every prescribed grid row, and that the BVA96 pathwise inequality is satisfied everywhere with this explicit source-exact error. The result follows from Proved BVA99 signed source residual integrability and Proved BVA97 true contact integrability. The key unresolved BVA96 mathematical obligation is solely to show the expected positive part of this exact canonical residual tends to zero across arbitrary supplied cofinal bands; that convergence is intentionally excluded here. No replacement process, finite-activity shortcut, false global generator L1 or artificial positive spatial error is used.

import Mathlib
